+++ b/docs/leased_delivery.rst
@@ -0,0 +1,23 @@
+Leased SQLite delivery
+======================
+
+SqliteHuey can reserve queued work until a consumer confirms completion.
+Call reserve_task(lease_for) to receive a token and a deserialized task. Execute
+the task with the existing API, then call ack_task(token) to remove its queue
+record. Execution does not acknowledge automatically. A live reservation can be
+renewed with renew_task or made immediately available with release_task.
+
+Lease deadlines use wall-clock epoch seconds, with optional explicit now values
+for deterministic coordination. Exactly at expiry, a task becomes eligible for a
+fresh reservation. Every reservation has a new token; expired or superseded
+tokens cannot acknowledge, renew or release current work. Pending counts and
+listings include leased work. Legacy dequeue skips live reservations.
+
+Reservations survive reopening the SQLite file. Existing databases gain the
+additional lease table without changing their tasks, results or schedules.
+create_tables=False still requires explicit initialize_schema. Immediate mode
+rejects the new APIs. Queue flushing removes this queue's reservations too.
+
+This is at-least-once delivery. A consumer can continue external work after its
+lease expires. Token fencing prevents stale queue acknowledgment, but external
+side effects still need their own idempotency policy.
